{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "05YR", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-spaces-hilbert}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d58b8b7340f0ac5824decd4b793094cc1e2f4a1f96300f5917f566d30b5fada9", "source_text": "Finite Hilbert stacks of spaces", "source_text_hash": "sha256:16d7a966ed61661ff95119eb0c3743d8d8b39fda8e1d558a1dbee6f5c34e0311", "unit_id": "tag:05YR:title"}
{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "05YR", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c07219fcbb0350eda041ccbe8f75cc2e92fca58a930fcce56221a1cc2ef5a292", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe finite Hilbert stack of an algebraic space is an algebraic stack.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:52b17ddc37b0c38186a56b37e022f06f7d64a62139b7da83966516cd8fbb5690", "unit_id": "tag:05YR:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "05YR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{H}_d(X)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-hilbert-stack-of-space}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:87d1e7f9f7d5bd1cc498d0f31ba04ab2c6b63a5a8aac0d19457ad6a0288feb20", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:de5dbb84ada680a7220ae96178e0c494c377a4574c6a8ccdb8c0a06d4d865da1", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nThen <MATH_0004> is an algebraic stack.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3ac8289dcc08d795a4239e935f32dc178881b54d3741c4d4cdacc12bb9839d02", "unit_id": "tag:05YS:statement"}
{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "05YR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$1$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\mathcal{H}_d(X) \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{H}_d\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{H}_d$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{H}_d(X)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-representable-on-top}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{proposition-finite-hilbert-point}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-representable-morphism-to-algebraic}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:96c9a09bbbe680283762e7f7a66cb3abfd70247243a6ee10cb1920ab249570c6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dead7e0ab4ff4658530c5bedd7957d0a13405bd3afc350a0811317112882a19c", "source_text": "The <MATH_0001>-morphism\n<MATH_0002>\nis representable by algebraic spaces according to\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nThe stack <MATH_0003> is an algebraic stack according to\nProposition <REF_0002>.\nHence <MATH_0004> is an algebraic stack by\nAlgebraic Stacks,\nLemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9b4693fa4922270b18f3d06021ae66b7a93b74c47ae92df815be376360024bf7", "unit_id": "tag:05YS:proof"}
{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "05YR", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c07219fcbb0350eda041ccbe8f75cc2e92fca58a930fcce56221a1cc2ef5a292", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis lemma allows us to bootstrap.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:040d2d8eb06a7f1d0608991007cb00a8b9979fda80dc07578e61eda94c36f652", "unit_id": "tag:05YR:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "05YR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$F : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$1$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$F$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}/\\mathcal{Y})$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-hilbert-stack-relative-space}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d5e7b2e8e5307ff1b58aced17bec448e4b38c2b656ed673089f4db9a63012b37", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4f642e29e8d8cf08f12b9cdcd420e114d785747e0d5bdb8a0aec194d0f8a9205", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a <MATH_0003>-morphism\nof stacks in groupoids over <MATH_0004> such that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0005> is representable by an algebraic space, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0006> is representable by algebraic spaces, surjective, flat, and\nlocally of finite presentation.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nThen <MATH_0007> is an algebraic stack.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:eb0b897f9c737f043f21f3ba9863f0b4153b63b467e1b2e752f13da8b56ab25b", "unit_id": "tag:06CI:statement"}
{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "05YR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$1$", "MATH_0004": "$f : \\mathcal{U} \\to \\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X})$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X})$", "MATH_0006": "$2$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\mathcal{W} =\n\\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}/\\mathcal{Y})\n\\times_{\\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}), f}\n\\mathcal{U}.\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{W}$", "MATH_0010": "$1$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{W} \\to \\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}/\\mathcal{Y})$", "MATH_0012": "$f$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{W}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0015": "$1$", "MATH_0016": "$$\n\\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}/\\mathcal{Y})\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}) \\times \\mathcal{Y}\n$$", "MATH_0017": "$2$", "MATH_0018": "$$\n\\mathcal{V} =\n\\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}/\\mathcal{Y})\n\\times_{(\\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}) \\times \\mathcal{Y}), f \\times F}\n(\\mathcal{U} \\times \\mathcal{X}).\n$$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{V} \\to \\mathcal{U} \\times \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0020": "$\\mathcal{V}$", "MATH_0021": "$1$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{V} \\to \\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0023": "$2$", "MATH_0024": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{V} \\ar[d] \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{X} \\ar[d]^F \\\\\n\\mathcal{W} \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{Y}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0025": "$$\n\\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}/\\mathcal{Y})\n\\times_{(\\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}) \\times \\mathcal{Y}), f \\times F}\n(\\mathcal{U} \\times \\mathcal{X})\n=\n(\\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}/\\mathcal{Y})\n\\times_{\\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}), f}\n\\mathcal{U}) \\times_{\\mathcal{Y}, F} \\mathcal{X}.\n$$", "MATH_0026": "$\\mathcal{V} \\to \\mathcal{W}$", "MATH_0027": "$F$", "MATH_0028": "$\\mathcal{V}$", "MATH_0029": "$\\mathcal{W}$", "MATH_0030": "$\\mathcal{W}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-hilbert-stack-of-space}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{examples-stacks-lemma-faithful-hilbert}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{stacks-lemma-2-fibre-product-gives-stack-in-setoids}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-base-change-representable-by-spaces}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-base-change-representable-transformations-property}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-smooth-surjective-morphism-implies-algebraic}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{lemma-flat-finite-presentation-surjective-diagonal}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{lemma-relative-hilbert}", "REF_0009": "\\ref{bootstrap-lemma-representable-by-spaces-over-space}", "REF_0010": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-base-change-by-space-representable-by-space}", "REF_0011": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-map-fibred-setoids-property}", "REF_0012": "\\ref{bootstrap-theorem-final-bootstrap}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7723a322fa9c41c39796150760eeab19bc458c856c775146326bf7c45213d569", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c9347e605ef1b8d7f7c3ad5a91ab730ed857e8b480c23ba063db236e878d08af", "source_text": "Choose a representable stack in groupoids <MATH_0001> over <MATH_0002> and a\n<MATH_0003>-morphism <MATH_0004>\nwhich is representable by algebraic spaces, smooth, and surjective.\nThis is possible because <MATH_0005> is an algebraic stack by\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nConsider the <MATH_0006>-fibre product\n<MATH_0007>\nSince <MATH_0008> is representable (in particular a stack in setoids)\nit follows from\nExamples of Stacks, Lemma <REF_0002>\nand\nStacks, Lemma <REF_0003>\nthat <MATH_0009> is a stack in setoids. The <MATH_0010>-morphism\n<MATH_0011> is\nrepresentable by algebraic spaces, smooth, and surjective as a base\nchange of the morphism <MATH_0012> (see\nAlgebraic Stacks,\nLemmas <REF_0004> and\n<REF_0005>).\nThus, if we can show that <MATH_0013> is representable by an algebraic space,\nthen the lemma follows from\nAlgebraic Stacks,\nLemma <REF_0006>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nThe diagonal of <MATH_0014> is representable by algebraic spaces according to\nLemma <REF_0007>.\nWe may apply\nLemma <REF_0008>\nto see that the <MATH_0015>-morphism\n<MATH_0016>\nis representable by algebraic spaces. Consider the <MATH_0017>-fibre product\n<MATH_0018>\nThe projection morphism <MATH_0019>\nis representable by algebraic spaces as a base change of the last\ndisplayed morphism. Hence <MATH_0020> is an algebraic space (see\nBootstrap, Lemma <REF_0009>\nor\nAlgebraic Stacks,\nLemma <REF_0010>).\nThe <MATH_0021>-morphism <MATH_0022> fits into the following\n<MATH_0023>-cartesian diagram\n<MATH_0024>\nbecause\n<MATH_0025>\nHence <MATH_0026> is representable by algebraic spaces,\nsurjective, flat, and locally of finite presentation as a base change\nof <MATH_0027>. It follows that the same thing is true for the corresponding\nsheaves of sets associated to <MATH_0028> and <MATH_0029>, see\nAlgebraic Stacks, Lemma <REF_0011>.\nThus we conclude that the sheaf associated to <MATH_0030> is an\nalgebraic space by\nBootstrap, Theorem <REF_0012>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8b69e27ea372696fd51a06aafccc6d6a58b00c602464176828ba8a18d1598284", "unit_id": "tag:06CI:proof"}
